//// ============================================
//// Domain Definitions
//// ============================================

//@Definition("verified-user", '''
//A user who has completed email verification.
//Represented by `User.isVerified == true`.

//## Requirements
//- Email verification link must be clicked
//- Verification expires after 24 hours
//- Re-verification required if email changes
//''')

//@Definition("soft-delete", '''
//Records are marked deleted but never physically removed.
//All entities have `deletedAt: datetime?` field.
//All queries filter `deletedAt == null` by default.
//''')

//// ============================================
//// Rules
//// ============================================

//@Rule("verification-required", '''
//All social features require `User.isVerified == true`.

//**No exceptions**, including:
//- Admin users
//- Test accounts
//- Internal users

//See @Definition("verified-user") for verification requirements.
//''')

//@Rule("message-retention", '''
//All messages must be retained for 7 years per compliance.
//Uses @Definition("soft-delete") pattern.
//''')

//// ============================================
//// Decisions
//// ============================================

//@Decision("no-group-messages", '''
//MVP does not support group messaging.

//**Considered:**
//1. Group messages - complex moderation, threading issues
//2. Channels (Slack-style) - significant scope increase
//3. 1:1 only - simple, covers core use case

//**Chose 1:1 only** because:
//- Faster to market
//- Simpler moderation
//- Can add groups in v2 if needed
//''')

//// ============================================
//// Open Questions
//// ============================================

//@OpenQuestion("message-encryption", '''
//Should messages be end-to-end encrypted?

//**Considerations:**
//- E2E: better privacy, but no server-side search/moderation
//- At-rest only: searchable, but less private

//**Stakeholders:** Security team, Legal
//**Decide by:** Before beta launch
//''')

